              "text": "**Mapping Bun and Node spawn**\n\nI’m comparing Bun's \"Bun.spawn\" to Node's \"child_process.spawn\" to create a direct mapping. The 'cmd: string[]' property in Node requires the first string as the command and an array of arguments. For instance, mapping 'cmd: [\"git\", \"status\"]' translates to 'spawn(\"git\", [\"status\"], { cwd, stdio: [\"inherit\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"], env })'. \n\nWith \"stdout: 'pipe'\" in Bun, Node handles it differently with the 'stdio' option. I need to consider the 'proc.exited' in Bun versus Node's 'await once(proc, \"close\")'. Node returns 'ChildProcess' with an 'exitCode' property, so I can use 'await new Promise(resolve => child.on(\"exit\", (code) => resolve(code)))' for handling exits."
