s: 'external' and explicitly externalize only the problematic packages.\n\n3) Full ESM bundle with Rollup/Vite SSR (best if you insist on bundling more)\n- Rollup handles mixed ESM/CJS better via @rollup/plugin-commonjs and dynamicRequireTargets, but you’ll still need to externalize some things.\n- Example Rollup setup:\n\n  import { builtinModules } from 'node:module'\n  import commonjs from '@rollup/plugin-commonjs'\n  import nodeResolve from '@rollup/plugin-node-resolve'\n  import json from '@rollup/plugin-json'\n\n  export default {\n    input: 'src/index.ts',\n    output: {\n      dir: 'dist',\n      format: 'esm',\n      sourcemap: true,\n      chunkFileNames: '[name]-[hash].mjs',\n    },\n    external: [\n      ...builtinModules,\n      /^node:/,\n      // Add specific deps here if they still explode during bundling\n      // 'isomorphic-git', 'some-cjs-only-lib',\n    ],\n    plugins: [\n      nodeResolve({\n        preferBuiltins: true,\n        exportConditions: ['node', 'import'],\n        extensions: ['.mjs', '.js', '.ts', '.json'],\n      }),\n      commonjs({\n        transformMixedEsModules: true,\n        // If you must support genuine dynamic require(), list files to inline:\n        // dynamicRequireTargets: ['node_modules/somepkg/lib/**/*.js']\n      }),\n      json(),\n    ],\n    treeshake: true,\n  }\n\n- This often works better than esbuild for mixed module trees, but you’ll still end up externalizing some deps.\n\n4) Single-file bundle (CJS output) by removing TLA\n- If a single artifact is mandatory, convert your entry to avoid top‑level await:\n\n  // before\n  const cfg = await loadConfig()\n  await startServer(cfg)\n\n  // after\n  async function main() {\n    const cfg = await loadConfig()\n    await startServer(cfg)\n  }\n  main().catch(err => {\n    console.error(err)\n    process.exit(1)\n  })\n\n- Then build with esbuild format: 'cjs'. import.meta.url in your source is fine; esbuild replaces it appropriately in CJS output.\n- This path has the highest compatibility with CJS-heavy deps.\n\nExtra knobs that often help\n- Prefer ESM code paths from deps:\n  - esbuild: mainFields: ['module', 'main'], conditions: ['node', 'import']\n  - rollup: nodeResolve({ exportConditions: ['node', 'import'] })\n- Always externalize Node built-ins: external: [/^node:/, ...builtinModules]\n- Where possible, upgrade deps to versions that publish ESM (execa is already ESM).\n\nWhat I’d do for your case (Node 22, Linux, local deploy)\n- If you don’t need a single-file artifact: Use option 1 or 2. I’d ship unbundled (option 1). If you want a leaner dist, use option 2: partial bundle your code to ESM and externalize node_modules.\n- If a single file is important: take option 4, remove TLA from the entry point and bundle to CJS with esbuild.\n\nTrying to fully bundle everything into a single ESM file with esbuild for a Node app that depends on CJS-y packages is where you’ll keep hitting “dynamic require” walls. Either externalize those packages or switch the final format to CJS (and drop TLA at the top level)."
